  "id": "COMPOUND:15395 - PROTEIN:5852",
  "verbalization": "Gamma-Glutamyltyramine is implicated in the interaction with BT-474 through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in the regulation of cellular processes. The evidence suggests that gamma-Glutamyltyramine acts as a target for multiple compounds, with VMRC-LCP being a common intermediate in these pathways. VMRC-LCP is a target of several compounds, including methyl 8-hydroxy-3,3-dimethyl-7H-pyrano[2,3-c]carbazole-10-carboxylate and (7E,9E,16Z)-18-hydroxyoctadeca-7,9,16-trien-11,13-diyn-4-one, which in turn target BT-474. This indicates a potential mechanism where gamma-Glutamyltyramine may influence BT-474 through these intermediates, possibly by modulating signaling pathways or cellular functions that are critical for the cell's survival or proliferation. The consistent presence of VMRC-LCP as a target across different compounds supports a unified mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
